1. CSV - CSV is a source data file containing raw business data extracted from a source system or operational process.
Example - Sales.csv, Customer.csv, Employee.csv

2. Staging - The staging layer is an intermediate layer where source data is landed and prepared for downstream transformation, while keeping close traceability to the source.
Example - No change in this layer, light transformation and standardization happens

3. Datawarehouse - A centralized repository designed to store integrated, historical and analytics-ready business data.
